{"timestamp": 1779342815.701775, "event_type": "meeting_called", "tick": 31, "data": {"caller": "player_0", "reason": "Alice called an emergency meeting", "bodies": [{"room": "security", "victim_name": "Charlie"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779342815.702413, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 31, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779342839.561857, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 31, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I called this because Charlie is dead in security. My route this round was cafeteria \u2192 medbay \u2192 storage \u2192 lower_engine \u2192 upper_engine \u2192 oxygen \u2192 back to cafeteria. I never went into security myself, and I didn\u2019t see Charlie alive at any point.\n\nEncounters: I saw Frank in lower_engine around tick 23. Then I saw Diana enter upper_engine from oxygen around tick 28. I didn\u2019t see either of them near security directly. Since Bob was ejected last meeting and the game didn\u2019t end, the Duck has to be either Diana or Frank now. I\u2019m not hard accusing yet, but we need to compare their routes carefully because Charlie died in security."}}
{"timestamp": 1779342857.1840909, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 31, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "My route was medbay \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 oxygen \u2192 upper_engine \u2192 lower_engine \u2192 storage \u2192 navigation. I saw Alice twice: at tick 12 she entered medbay from cafeteria, and at tick 23 she entered lower_engine from storage while I was there. That matches what she\u2019s saying about her route, at least for those points.\n\nI did not see Diana at all this round, and I never went into security. I also didn\u2019t see Charlie alive or the body.\n\nFrom my perspective, Alice\u2019s route is partially confirmed by me, and Diana is the only person I have zero info on. But I\u2019ll be honest: Alice could technically still have had time through medbay/electrical/security depending on timing, so I don\u2019t want to blindly clear anyone. Diana needs to give a very specific route and explain whether she was near security. Since it\u2019s between Diana and Alice from my view, I\u2019m leaning Diana right now unless her story is strong."}}
{"timestamp": 1779342881.692472, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 31, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Alice, I\u2019m really stuck on one thing: how do you know Charlie is dead *in security* if you never went into security and didn\u2019t report the body? That sounds like exact body-location knowledge, not emergency info.\n\nMy route was mostly east/center: navigation \u2192 weapons \u2192 cafeteria/medbay/electrical area, then cafeteria \u2192 oxygen \u2192 upper_engine. Alice is right that she saw me come into upper_engine from oxygen near the end. I never saw Frank this round, and I didn\u2019t see Charlie\u2019s body.\n\nFrank\u2019s route at least has Alice confirming parts of it, but Alice\u2019s statement is the weirdest to me. If she \u201cnever went into security,\u201d then saying \u201cCharlie is dead in security\u201d feels like a slip. I\u2019m leaning Alice unless she can explain exactly how she knew that."}}
{"timestamp": 1779342908.2121332, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 31, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "Diana is right to call that out \u2014 I need to correct myself clearly: I did **not** see Charlie\u2019s body and I cannot actually confirm the body was in security. That was a bad statement from me, not an observation. What I know for sure is Charlie was dead when the meeting started, and I called the button from cafeteria.\n\nMy confirmed route is still cafeteria \u2192 medbay \u2192 storage \u2192 lower_engine \u2192 upper_engine \u2192 oxygen \u2192 cafeteria. Frank saw me at medbay/lower_engine timing, and I saw Diana come from oxygen into upper_engine near the end.\n\nThe important thing is: Diana\u2019s own route puts her in the east side \u2014 navigation/weapons/electrical/security area \u2014 much closer to where a security kill *could* have happened than my route or Frank\u2019s claimed route. I agree my wording was bad, but based on routes and opportunity, I\u2019m still much more suspicious of Diana than Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779342940.708334, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 31, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I want to be really careful here because one wrong vote probably loses us the game.\n\nWhat I can confirm: I saw Alice enter medbay from cafeteria at tick 12, and I saw her enter lower_engine from storage at tick 23. That supports parts of her route, but it does **not** fully clear her for the whole round.\n\nDiana\u2019s route is definitely near the east side \u2014 navigation/weapons/security/electrical area \u2014 so if Charlie really died in security, Diana had opportunity. But the problem is: the **only** person who said \u201cCharlie is dead in security\u201d was Alice, and Alice called button from cafeteria, not a body report. I don\u2019t see how Alice could know that location if she never went there and didn\u2019t see the body.\n\nSo to me, that location slip is stronger evidence than route proximity. Diana is suspicious for being vague and being near that side, but Alice\u2019s statement sounds like hidden information. I\u2019m leaning Alice right now unless there\u2019s some explanation I\u2019m missing."}}
